<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait April bank assets ease month/month.</title>
<headline>Kuwait April bank assets ease month/month.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Combined assets of banks operating in Kuwait fell slightly to 11.807 billion dinars at the end of April from 11.816 billion at the end of March, Central Bank said in a monthly bulletin.</p>
<p>Assets were 11.065 billion dinars in April 1996.</p>
<p>			Figures in million Kuwaiti dinars</p>
<p>					April '97   March '97   April '96</p>
<p> Cash				    34.6	   44.8	 83.1</p>
<p> Balances with Central Bank	27.9	   26.8	 12.1</p>
<p> Public debt instruments	1,650.7	1,684.3    1,871.7</p>
<p> Debt purchase bonds	    2,701.4	2,716.0    3,216.8</p>
<p> Other local investments	  302.4	  295.2	329.4</p>
<p>Credit facilities to</p>
<p>  residents			 3,479.1	3,456.0    2,624.4</p>
<p> Foreign assets		   2,264.6	2,294.7    2,007.9</p>
<p> Inter bank local deposits	820.4	  748.2	462.8</p>
<p> Other assets			 525.4	  549.5	456.8</p>
<p> Total			     11,806.6     11,815.6   11,064.9</p>
<p>Note: Data covers eight commercial and specialised banks, the Islamic institution Kuwait Finance House and a Kuwaiti branch of a Bahrain-based bank.</p>
<p>Debt purchase bonds include the value of the purchase by the government of the real estate portfolio of Kuwait Finance House in December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.302 dinar)</p>
<p>-- Inal Ersan, +965 243-1920</p>
